# End-of-RIB for a family that carried no route.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 4724 Section 4 -- "The End-of-RIB marker MUST be sent by a BGP
#            speaker to its peer once it completes the initial routing update
#            (including the case when there is no update to send) for an address
#            family after the BGP session is established". ipv4/unicast carries a
#            route here and ipv6/unicast carries none; both get their marker.
# PREVENTS:  the reading that ze sends End-of-RIB only for families that carried
#            routes. test/plugin/eor-per-family.ci proves the two-family case with NO routes
#            at all, where every family is silent and the two readings agree. This
#            is the fixture that tells them apart.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE, measured rather than assumed: it does not isolate WHICH
# producer emitted the ipv6 marker. sendInitialRoutes is one; AnnounceEOR
# (internal/component/bgp/reactor/reactor_api_forward.go) is another, and its
# suppression only holds while the peer is still draining its initial route sync.
# Narrowing the sendInitialRoutes loop to route-carrying families leaves this test
# GREEN across three consecutive runs, because the second path still delivers the
# marker. The test that pins the producer is the unit one:
# TestInitialSyncEORReachesTheSilentFamilyToo in
# internal/component/bgp/reactor/peer_initial_sync_test.go, which asserts on the
# bytes sendInitialRoutes itself puts on the socket and goes red under exactly that
# narrowing. Read the two together; neither is the whole claim.
#
# Marker hex: ipv4/unicast is a minimum-length UPDATE; every other family is an
# UPDATE carrying only MP_UNREACH_NLRI for its <AFI, SAFI> (RFC 4724 Section 2).
# Both are copied from test/plugin/eor-per-family.ci, which derives them from exabgp.
#
# The route frame at seq=1, field by field: 16 marker octets, length 0x0031 = 49,
# type 02 = UPDATE, withdrawn-routes-length 0x0000, path-attribute-length 0x0015 =
# 21, then ORIGIN IGP (40 01 01 00), an empty AS_PATH (40 02 00), NEXT_HOP 10.0.0.1
# (40 03 04 0A000001) and LOCAL_PREF 100 (40 05 04 00000064) = 4+3+7+7 = 21, then
# the NLRI 193.0.2.1/32 (20 C1000201) = 5. 16+2+1+2+2+21+5 = 49.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00310200000015400101004002004003040A0000014005040000006420C1000201
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=3:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF001E0200000007900F0003000201
EOF_PEER

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
				ipv6/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				next-hop 10.0.0.1
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 193.0.2.1/32
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
